(e) 5",": In order for the digits of a number to add up to 2, the digits must be either one 2 and the
rest zeros, or two 1s and the rest zeros. Since no prime number can have a 0 in the ones place, and 1
is not considered a prime number, the only candidates are 2, 11, 101 and 1001. Out of those, 2, 11 and
101 are indeed primes, however, 1001 = 910 + 91 = 11 \cdot 91, so it is not a prime.",208aaa
