2009_level2_solutions.pdf,25,d,"A square is cut into three rectangles along two lines parallel to a side, as shown. If
the perimeters of of the three rectangles are 22, 26 and 24, respectively, then the
area of the original square is
(a) 24
(b) 36
(c) 64
(d) 81
(e) 96",": Let's call the widths of the three rectangles x, y and z. Then the side
of the square is x +y +z, and the perimeters of the rectangles are 2x +2(x +y +z),
2y + 2(x + y + z) and 2z + 2(x + y + z). These have to be equal to 22, 26 and 24. This gives us a system
of equations
2x + y + z = 11
x + 2y + z = 13
x + y + 2z = 12
Adding these three equations together gives us 4x + 4y + 4z = 36 or x + y + z = 9. Therefore the side of
the square is 9, and the area is 81.",215aaa
