(e) none of the above
The answer is: (d)","1: This can be done just by checking that only (d) f(x) = x2 + 2x + 1
passes through the 3 given points. In fact, f(0) = 1, f(1) = 4 and f(2) = 9.
Solution 2: Let f(x) = ax2 + bx + c be the equation of the parabola. We are given
f(0) = 1 ( i.e., c = 1), f(1) = 4 and f(2) = 9. The two last equations give the
system:
a + b + 1 = 4,
4a + 2b + 1 = 9.
Solving it gives a = 1 and b = 2. Hence f(x) = x2 + 2x + 1.
