case, when he switches, he is assured of choosing a door with no prize.
Contestant's first choice has a 2/3 chance of being a ""no prize"" door. If this is the case,
when he switches, he is assured of choosing the door with the prize, because the other ""no
prize"" door has been eliminated by the host.
Hence if the contestant switches doors, the probability he gets the prize is 1/3(0)+2/3(1) =
2/3.",306aaa
