Solution: \bigtriangleupPMN, \bigtriangleupKLP and \bigtriangleupSPR are similar triangles. We shall use that
if we have two similar triangles with the ratio of linear elements (such as lengths
of sides etc.) equal to \lambda, then the ratio of their areas is \lambda2. Let PN = x, PK =
y and SR = z.
From the similarity it follows, y = 5/3x and z = 3x.
