coefficient is (x + y + z)/x = 17/3. So the areas satisfy the relation A(\bigtriangleupABC) =
(17/3)2A(\bigtriangleupPMN) = 172 = 289.",331aaa
2012_MO_L1Sol.pdf,18,,"Nine scientists are working on a secret project.
They wish to lock up the
documents in a cabinet so that the cabinet can be opened when and only when five
or more of the scientists are present. For this purpose a certain number of locks
are installed on the cabinet and each of the scientists is given keys to some of these
locks. Each key can open exactly one lock. Thus, for the cabinet to be opened (i)
any five of the scientists have to be present and (ii) the keys to all of the locks on
the cabinet have to be among the set of all keys given to the present five scientists.
What is the smallest number of locks needed?
(a) 126
