2013_MO_L1Sol.pdf,16,,"For how many integers n between 1 and 100 does x2 + x -n factor into the
product of two linear factors with integer coefficients?
(a) 9
(b) 2
(c) 1
(d) 10
(e) none of the above
The answer is: (a)","1: Since -n < 0, it follows that x2 + x -n = (x -a)(x + b) where a and
b are positive integers. Thus n = ab and b = 1 + a by expanding the right hand side
of the above equality. Here are the possible choices for a and b:
a: 1 --- 2 ---. . .--- 9 --- 10
b: 2 --- 3 ---. . .--- 10 --- 11
n = ab: 1 \cdot 2 = 2 --- 2 \cdot 3 = 6--- . . . ---9 \cdot 10 = 90 --- 10 \cdot 11 = 110.
There are 9 values for n between 1 and 100.
Solution 2: By the quadratic formula, x2 + x -n = (x -x1)(x -x2) where
x1, x2 = -1 \pm \sqrt{1} + 4n
