2013_MO_L2Sol.pdf,5,,"The Bayes family has two cars. One of them has a 90% chance of starting on any given
morning, and the other has an 80% chance. On any given morning, what is the probability
that at least one of the cars will start?
(a) .72
(b) .9
(c) .7
(d) .98
(e) none of the above
The answer is: (d)","The probability that the first car won't start is .1. The probability that the
second car won't start is .2. So the probability that they both fail to start is .02. (We
assume the events are independent.) At least one starting is the complement of both failing,
so the probability that at least one starts is 1 -.02 = .98.",393aaa
