The answer is: (b)","If x < 0 the equation has no solution. So, let x \ge0. If \sqrt{3} + x > x, then
3 + \sqrt{3} + x > 3 + x, and
\sqrt
3 + \sqrt{3} + x > \sqrt{3} + x > x. Add 3 to the outer parts of the last
