2014_MO_L2Sol.pdf,11,,"The function f(x) satisfies the equation f(x) = f(x -1) + f(x + 1) for all values of x.
If f(1) = 1 and f(2) = 3, what is the value of f(2014)?
(a) 3
(b) 1
(c) -1
(d) -3
(e) none of the above
The answer is: (c)","Since f(x) = f(x-1)+f(x+1), then f(x+1) = f(x)-f(x-1), and so f(1) = 1
f(2) = 3
f(3) = f(2) -f(1) = 3 -1 = 2
f(4) = f(3) -f(2) = 2 -3 = -1
f(5) = f(4) -f(3) = -1 -2 = -3
f(6) = f(5) -f(4) = -3 -(-1) = -2
f(7) = f(6) -f(5) = -2 -(-3) = 1 = f(1)
f(8) = f(7) -f(6) = 1 -(-2) = 3 = f(2)
Since the value of f at an integer depends only on the values of f at the two previous integers,
then the fact that the first several values form a cycle with f(7) = f(1) and f(8) = f(2) tells
us that the values of f will always repeat in sets of 6. Since 2014 is 4 more than a multiple
of 6 (as 2014 = 4 + 2010 = 4 + 6(335)), then f(2014) = f(2014 -6(335)) = f(4) = -1.",450aaa
