What is the value of a + b + c + d?
(a) 19
(b) 18
(c) 17
(d) 16
(e) none of the above
The answer is: (b)","dding the two equations, we obtain
ac + bd + ad + bc = 77
ac + ad + bc + bd = 77
a(c + d) + b(c + d) = 77
(a + b)(c + d) = 77
Since each of a, b, c and d is a positive integer, then a + b and c + d are each positive
integers and are each at least 2. Since the product of a + b and c + d is 77 = 7 \times 11 (with
7 and 11 both prime), then one must equal 7 and the other must equal 11.
Therefore,
a + b + c + d = 7 + 11 = 18. (We can check with some work that (a, b, c, d) = (5, 2, 4, 7) is a
solution to the system.)",457aaa
