(d) 7
(e) p(x) = 0 has no solution
The answer is: (a)","We have, after factorization, p(x) = (x3 + 2x -3)(x -1 + x -5) =
(x3 +2x-3)(2x-6) = (x-1)(x2 +x+3)(2x-6). (Note that 1 is an obvious root of
x3+2x-3, so if we use long division by x-1, we get x3+2x-3 = (x-1)(x2+x+3).)
Since x2 + x + 3 has no real roots since it has a negative discriminant, thus the sum
of roots of p(x) = 0 is 3 + 1 = 4.",477aaa
2015_MO_L1Sol.pdf,16,,"Given that (x, y) satisfies x2 + y2 = 9, what is the largest possible value of
x2 + 3y2 + 4x?
(a) 22
(b) 24
(c) 36
(d) 27
(e) 29
The answer is: (e)","Replace y2 with 9 -x2 and then complete the square to get x2 -3x2 +
27 + 4x = 29 -2x2 + 4x -2 = 29 -2(x -1)2, which is at most 29.",478aaa
2015_MO_L1Sol.pdf,17,,"Mr. and Mrs. Alpha, Mr. and Mrs. Beta, and Mr. and Mrs. Gamma are
standing in a line. How many ways are there line them up so that none of them are
standing next to their spouse?
(a) 144
(b) 240
(c) 288
(d) 432
(e) none of the above
The answer is: (b)","There are 6 ways to pick the first person in the line. Then there are four
ways to pick the next person as it can't be the same as the first person, or be the
spouse of that person. Then there are two things that can happen with the third
choice. If the third person in line is the spouse of the first person, the fourth person
cannot be the spouse of the second person, or that will leave the last couple at the
end, so there are two choices for the fourth person, it must be either the husband or
wife of the couple that hasn't been used yet, but exactly one choice for each of the
fifth and sixth person since the fifth person must be the spouse of the second person.
If the third person is not the spouse of the first person and is from the remaining
couple, then there are two choices for the fourth person, and in this case there will
be two choices for the fifth person. Since there are two ways this can happen there
are 8 cases here. So altogether there are 10 different ways to pick the third, fourth,
6

SVSU 2015 Math Olympics
Solutions Level I-page 7 of 11
fifth, and sixth places in the line. So there are 6 \times 4 \times 10 = 240 different ways to
line them up.",479aaa
2015_MO_L1Sol.pdf,18,,"The sides of a right triangle are a, 2a + 2d and 2a + 3d, with a and d both
positive. The ratio of a to d is:
(a) 5:1
(b) 27:2
(c) 4:1
(d) 1:5
(e) none of the above
The answer is: (a)","For the right triangle, the longest side is the hypotenuse, therefore a2 +
(2a + 2d)2 = (2a + 3d)2. So a2 + (4a2 + 8ad + 4d2) = 4a2 + 12ad + 9d2 and we have
a2 -4ad -5d2 = 0. Factorization yields (a -5d)(a + d) = 0 implying a = 5d or
a = -d (dropped since both a and d > 0). Hence a : d = 5d : d = 5 : 1.",480aaa
