(e) x > 1",": If x2-1 and x2-9 are both positive, ||x2 -1||+||x2 -9|| = x2-1+x2-9 = 2x2-10.
If x2 -1 and x2 -9 are both negative ||x2 -1|| + ||x2 -9|| = -(x2 -1) -(x2 -9) = -2x2 + 10.
If x2 -1 is positive and x2 -9 is negative, |||x2 -1||| + |||x2 -9||| = x2 -1 -(x2 -9) = -1 + 9 = 8.
x2 -1 is positive when x < -1 or x > 1, x2 -9 is negative when -3 < x < 3. So to have x2 -1
is positive and x2 -9 is negative, we must have -3 < x < -1 or 1 < x < 3.",496aaa
