(b) 72{\textopenbullet}
(c) 78{\textopenbullet}
(d) 82{\textopenbullet}
(e) None of the above",": Each minute, the minute hand moves (360/60){\textopenbullet}= 6{\textopenbullet}clockwise, and the hour
hand moves (360/720){\textopenbullet}= (1/2){\textopenbullet}. At 7:24 pm, the hour hand moved (7\cdot60+24)\cdot(1/2){\textopenbullet}= 222{\textopenbullet}
from its top position while the minute hand moved 24 \cdot 6{\textopenbullet}= 144{\textopenbullet}from its top position. The
angle between the two hands is 222{\textopenbullet}-144{\textopenbullet}-78{\textopenbullet}.

