(d) 17
(e) 45",": Factor the second equation and use the first equation. We have x3 + y 3 = (x +
y)(x2-xy +y 2) = 3(x2-xy +y 2) = 117. Therefore 39 = x2-xy +y 2 = (x+y)2-3xy = 9-3xy.
