(e) more than three solutions",": Using properties of logarithms, the equation can be rewritten as 2 log x = (log x)2.
Substituting u = log x gives us 2u = u2 or 2u -u2 = 0 or u(2 -u) = 0, which means that u = 0 or
u = 2. That gives us x = 1 or x = 200.",680aaa
